<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huhanye</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">submitted <a href="/years/51-bce">51 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huhanye was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanyu">chanyu</a>, or supreme ruler, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-xiongnu">Southern Xiongnu</a> during the succession conflicts of the mid-first century BCE. In 51 BCE he submitted to Han suzerainty, travelling in person to the Han court in exchange for protection and trade privileges. His submission split the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> and marked a turning point in the decline of the Xiongnu Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huhanye.jpg" alt="Huhanye" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: de:User:Postmann Michael · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hsiung-nu-Empire.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
